Appendix E – Validation Protocol and Ablation Study (Complete)

E.1 Simulation Configuration

· Physics: MuJoCo XLA with soft-body extension, contact parameters tuned to match gel deformation curves.
· Rendering: Isaac Sim with TACTO plugin: 320×240 resolution, non‑linear elastomer response, pixel saturation at high strain, structured noise as described.
· Robot Model: UR5e with joint-level friction and backlash (0.2° deadband); LEAP Hand with underactuated tendon compliance.

E.2 Benchmark Tasks – Detailed Protocol

Task A: Cable Threading (DLO)

· Object: 30 cm cable, diameter 8 mm, bending stiffness varied from 0.01 to 0.5 Nm².
· Procedure: The robot grasps one end of the cable, lifts it, and must insert the tip through a 1 cm hole at 20 cm height. Success requires the cable not to buckle or snag.
· Evaluation: 30 trials per stiffness range; compare θ estimation error (relative to ground truth), success rate.

Task B: Cloth Folding (DSO)

· Object: Cotton (density 0.3 g/cm³) and silk (0.1 g/cm³) squares, 30×30 cm.
· Procedure: The robot picks the cloth from a table, performs a sequence of folds to quarter it. Force must stay within ±0.5 N of the cloth’s typical resistance to avoid tearing.
· Probing budget: 0.5 s allowed for probing before each fold; total budget 2 s. If exceeded, system runs with default mean stiffness.
· Metrics: IoU of final fold, probing time used, number of residual monitor triggers (chattering events).

Task C: Strawberry Grasping

· Object: Simulated strawberry, 50 g, non‑uniform stiffness (soft spots 0.1 N/mm, firm spots 0.8 N/mm), bruising threshold 2 N.
· Procedure: Pick from a bin with 10 distractors; move to a location without dropping.
· Metrics: Unmitigated force violations (counts), success (berry intact), reflex frequency.

E.3 Ablation Study Design

Condition Modules Purpose
VTSM‑Full Encoder (with domain adapt.) + iSVD PE ID + guided consistency policy + reflex Baseline
No‑Synesthesia Vision‑only encoder, no tactile hallucination Remove anticipatory perception
No‑ID Default mean stiffness, no probe or estimation Remove material adaptation
No‑Guidance λ_guide = 0, no safety gradient in policy Remove probabilistic safety bias

Each condition is tested on all tasks, 30 seeds each. Paired t‑tests compare performance. Hypothesis: each ablation degrades performance on the specific task that relies most on the removed module.

E.4 Few‑Shot Adaptation Experiment (Path to Generality)

To demonstrate extensibility, after main training:

· Choose a hold‑out task: folding a paper airplane (complex folding sequence, different material).
· Provide 10 teleoperated demonstrations.
· Fine‑tune only the policy head (consistency model conditioning layers) for 20 epochs, while freezing encoder and safety modules.
